## How to use this script
To use this script, copy this R Markdown file to a local directory to your analysis such as the pipeline processing directory ([DIR]). This can then either be knitted directly in RStudio or run through the command line as part of a pipeline. The following parameters are needed:

``` {r, eval = FALSE, echo = TRUE}
experiment_title = The title to be included in the report. If knitting directly, this must be added in the header above.
user_name        = The user name to be included in the report. If knitting directly, this must be added in the header above.
analysis_dir     = The directory where the results will be stored. It is recommended to always start with an empty output directory.
experiment_type  = One of "illumina" or "nanopore".
load_type        = Should the input data files be pulled from the "pipeline" or "input".
experiment_code  = The experiment code from the pipeline. Required if load_type == "pipeline".
process_num      = The processing number from the pipeline. Required if load_type == "pipeline".
indir            = The Directory containing the necessary input files. Required if load_type == "input".
min_otus         = The minimum number of OTUs for filtered samples in the final rarefied data set (recommended 10000).
nclass           = The number of individual taxa to show on barplots (recommended 15).
group_cols       = A named vector of colours with colors specific to your group names.
test_type        = Should parametric tests be used for the analyses. One of "parametric" or "non-parametric".
control          = The level for Group to be used as the control samples.
otu_or_asv       = Do the total taxa counts represent "OTU" or "ASV" counts?
read_type        = Which data was used for the analysis? One of "raw", "trim" or "filter".
rep_shapes       = The manual point values to use for the replicates.
```

