# Section 8: Sensitivity Analysis

In our primary analysis, we included individuals who had self reported to have taken NSAIDS within the last week prior to the 6MSM. We also included individuals who reported gastrointestinal (GI) obstructive disease or GI surgery. NSAIDS are reported to have an effect on the composition of the gut microbiota [paper link here](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1198743X15009027?via%3Dihub). GI obstructive disease or suregery are often used as exclusion criteria within human microbiome studies. However, they be putative risk factors given the highlighted role og the GI system  in exertional heat illness aetiology.  As such, we performed sensitivity analysis. We removed individuals who reported NSAID use (n=13) within the last week and individuals who reported GI obstructive disease or GI surgery (n=1) from our cohort. We also excluded the respective pair matched case or control. 13 pairs were removed. The UIN who reported GI disease or GI surgery, alos reported NSAID use. Below is a summary of UINs that reported NSAID use and/or GI disease or GI surgery:

``` {r Section8_sen_data}
